---
import PathwayLandingLayout from '../../layouts/PathwayLandingLayout.astro';
import { getPathwayHero } from '@/lib/pathwayHeroes';
import { SITE_CONFIG } from '@/lib/seo/config';
import { TEA_INVESTMENT_THRESHOLD } from '@/lib/eb5-investment';

const title = 'EB-5 Visa for Taiwanese Investors | StudentEB5';
const metaDescription =
  'EB-5 for Taiwanese investors covers investment basics, student timing, and family funding considerations for Taiwan-born nationals evaluating a U.S. green card through EB-5.';
const canonicalUrl = `${SITE_CONFIG.url}/pathways/eb5-for-taiwanese-investors`;
const h1 = 'EB-5 Visa for Taiwanese Investors';
const subhead =
  'A single overview for Taiwanese nationals (investors, students, and families) evaluating EB-5 as a path to permanent residence.';

const teaFormatted = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {
  style: 'currency',
  currency: 'USD',
  maximumFractionDigits: 0,
}).format(TEA_INVESTMENT_THRESHOLD);

const relatedResearch = [
  {
    title: 'EB-5 Immigrant Investor Program: Complete Guide',
    url: '/research/complete-2027-eb5-guide',
    description: 'Filing steps, rural set-asides, and current program structure overview.',
  },
  {
    title: 'EB-5 Investment Process',
    url: '/eb5-investment-process',
    description: 'Step-by-step filing sequence from source of funds through I-829.',
  },
];
const hero = getPathwayHero('eb5-for-taiwanese-investors');

---

<PathwayLandingLayout
  title={title}
  metaDescription={metaDescription}
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
  h1={h1}
  subhead={subhead}
  heroImage={hero.image}
  heroImageWebp={hero.webp}
  heroImageAlt="EB-5 pathway for Taiwanese investors"
  relatedResearch={relatedResearch}
  secondaryCtaText="Talk to Someone About EB-5 for Taiwanese Nationals"
  breadcrumbTitle="EB-5 for Taiwanese Investors"
  keywords={[
    'EB-5 for Taiwanese investors',
    'EB-5 Taiwan',
    'Taiwanese nationals EB-5',
    'EB-5 visa Taiwan',
  ]}
>
  <Fragment slot="extraCompliance">
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed border border-border rounded-lg bg-secondary/40 p-4 m-0">
      EB-5 investment involves financial risk, including potential loss of principal, and does not guarantee a green
      card, visa availability, or any specific processing time. Consult a qualified immigration attorney and a
      FINRA-registered financial adviser for guidance specific to your situation.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <p>
    The EB-5 Immigrant Investor Program offers eligible foreign nationals a path to a U.S. green card through a
    qualifying investment. Taiwanese nationals (investors abroad, students in the U.S., and families considering gifted
    capital) work within the same program framework: investment threshold, source-of-funds documentation, project
    selection, and I-526E filing. Visa allocation follows country of birth; confirm current availability on the
    <a
      href="https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/legal/visa-law0/visa-bulletin.html"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">Visa Bulletin</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>For investors</h2>
  <p>
    Most investors use the reduced Targeted Employment Area (TEA) investment threshold of {teaFormatted}, which covers
    capital only. After documenting lawful source of funds and selecting a project, investors file Form I-526E,
    often with concurrent adjustment of status when already in the U.S. on valid nonimmigrant status. For the full
    sequence, see the
    <a href="/eb5-investment-process">EB-5 investment process</a> and the
    <a href="/research/complete-2027-eb5-guide">complete EB-5 guide</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>For students</h2>
  <p>
    Taiwanese F-1 students sometimes evaluate EB-5 alongside OPT/STEM OPT and H-1B planning. Filing EB-5 does not
    automatically convert F-1 status into permanent residence; it is a separate process. Preparing source-of-funds and
    gift documentation while still enrolled can reduce pressure later in the work-authorization window. Overview:
    <a href="/pathways/f1-to-eb5-self-sponsored-green-card">F-1 to EB-5 self-sponsored green card</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>For families funding an investment</h2>
  <p>
    When parents gift funds to a child who is the investor of record, USCIS still requires a clear lawful trail from the
    original source through the gift and into the investment. Cross-border tax and remittance planning should be handled
    with qualified advisers before capital moves. Funding-path options are summarized in
    <a href="/research/ways-to-fund-eb5-investment-2026">ways to fund an EB-5 investment</a>.
  </p>
</PathwayLandingLayout>
